#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092307 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a06fde5-14f9-5285-b92d-f08820423ff8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Containing a Hyperbolic Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68c94a48-272c-5bc2-926d-631b27cfaa45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No real solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089458} {:answer/id #uuid "099be20b-5e48-564f-98f5-28d7ecf6b8b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506694} {:answer/id #uuid "1d312a4b-6494-5399-99d8-2711c306406d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506734} {:answer/id #uuid "665c592f-073e-5831-84b5-852831d2f92c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506920} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e94f21-5291-5486-b32e-6255c6ada160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "099be20b-5e48-564f-98f5-28d7ecf6b8b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506694} :answer-field/id #uuid "d624565d-12d3-5a45-a9fe-696c0efd0999" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65da3929-a610-575c-ac56-f7fecd19aa73" :question/math-academy-id "q-138673" :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation $5\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=4.$" :question/worked-solution "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above definition into the equation $5\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\cdot (\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}) & =4 \\\\ 5({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) & =4({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}) \\\\ 5{e}^{x}-5{e}^{-x} & =4{e}^{x}+4{e}^{-x} \\\\ {e}^{x} & =9{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply both sides of the equation by ${e}^{x}$ and solve the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{x} & ={e}^{x}\\cdot 9{e}^{-x} \\\\ {e}^{2x} & =9 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡9 \\\\ 2x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡9 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡9 \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({9}^{1/2}) \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only real solution is $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092307 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a06fde5-14f9-5285-b92d-f08820423ff8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Containing a Hyperbolic Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec708962-ad6c-5d78-85a9-f0cb925fa107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\left(\\frac{9}{7}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec708962-ad6c-5d78-85a9-f0cb925fa107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\left(\\frac{9}{7}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507201} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b282f9b-5bb1-5f62-87e7-540c34e64d8c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d9591085-98d5-5c4b-b445-1e12f9553b30" :question/math-academy-id "q-342996" :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation $8\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=1.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above definition into the equation $8\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8(\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}) & =1 \\\\ 8({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) & ={e}^{x}+{e}^{-x} \\\\ 8{e}^{x}-8{e}^{-x} & ={e}^{x}+{e}^{-x} \\\\ 7{e}^{x} & =9{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply both sides of the equation by ${e}^{x}$ and solve the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot 7{e}^{x} & ={e}^{x}\\cdot 9{e}^{-x} \\\\ {e}^{2x} & =\\frac{9}{7} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{9}{7}) \\\\ 2x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{9}{7}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{9}{7})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only real solution is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{9}{7}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507481 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4e30c14-d6f7-5585-bad2-4ddff6ed297f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Containing Multiple Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b25fc98-6b4b-5cd1-9cd3-43b869cd7a33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b25fc98-6b4b-5cd1-9cd3-43b869cd7a33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506818} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ac201d2-a792-512b-8f92-08f810b6da8d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ad0a1bc0-aba6-5fee-bd17-2613e12ebda4" :question/math-academy-id "q-343010" :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=7.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The definitions of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}),\\,\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above definitions into the equation $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=7,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})+\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) & =7 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x} & =7 \\\\ {e}^{x} & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x} & =7 \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)$ is the only real solution to the equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507415 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4e30c14-d6f7-5585-bad2-4ddff6ed297f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Containing Multiple Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8717b52d-c98b-5827-ae6e-a4aae8cc0bc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8717b52d-c98b-5827-ae6e-a4aae8cc0bc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506976} :answer-field/id #uuid "94388d20-3ee6-5d86-8e2a-77d7bfe36af0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35b119d2-4fa9-5b4b-9344-68f1ddad4e3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-343016" :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+5\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=5.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The definitions of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}),\\,\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above definitions into the equation $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+5\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})+5\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})) & =5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})+\\frac{5}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) & =5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x}+\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{x}-\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-x} & =5 \\\\ 3{e}^{x}-2{e}^{-x} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply both sides of the equation by ${e}^{x},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot (3{e}^{x}-2{e}^{-x}) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot 5 \\\\ 3{e}^{2x}-2 & =5{e}^{x} \\\\ 3{e}^{2x}-5{e}^{x}-2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a quadratic equation in ${e}^{x}$ that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3{e}^{x}+1)({e}^{x}-2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the zero-product property, we have to solve two equations:\n\n$$\n3{e}^{x}+1=0,\\,{e}^{x}-2=0.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{x}+1 & =0 &  & \\, & {e}^{x}-2 & =0 \\\\ 3{e}^{x} & =-1 &  & \\, & {e}^{x} & =2 \\\\ {e}^{x} & =-\\frac{1}{3} &  & \\, & x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no real values of $x$ for which ${e}^{x}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ Therefore, the only real solution to the equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507514 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4e30c14-d6f7-5585-bad2-4ddff6ed297f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Containing Multiple Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08959185-7ae8-545f-a27e-c6317b14d655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506692} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd24afb-2e8a-5315-bf56-83e7629e3b50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})$ and $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506822} {:answer/id #uuid "42bb5a15-e42c-5fde-b8fd-dab42d65178f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=0$ and $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506834} {:answer/id #uuid "8306f30c-7d39-5a1a-8a33-fa06c26a37c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506969} {:answer/id #uuid "b943a61a-5fba-553b-ba34-318ed7a58bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42bb5a15-e42c-5fde-b8fd-dab42d65178f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=0$ and $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506834} :answer-field/id #uuid "93460c70-4a67-59ae-ac0f-2d86b0582d6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dc0cc655-da41-5f5b-b054-719fe2ce042d" :question/math-academy-id "q-9675" :question/problem "Find the real solutions to the equation $5\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=5.$" :question/worked-solution "The definitions of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}),\\,\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above definitions into the equation  $5\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}))-\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) & =5 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{e}^{x}+\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x} & =5 \\\\ 2{e}^{x}+3{e}^{-x} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply both sides of the equation by ${e}^{x},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot (2{e}^{x}+3{e}^{-x}) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot 5 \\\\ 2{e}^{2x}+3 & =5{e}^{x} \\\\ 2{e}^{2x}-5{e}^{x}+3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a quadratic equation in ${e}^{x}$ that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{e}^{x}-3)({e}^{x}-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the zero-product property, we have to solve two equations:\n\n$$\n2{e}^{x}-3=0,\\,{e}^{x}-1=0\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{x}-3 & =0 &  & \\, & {e}^{x}-1 & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x} & =\\frac{3}{2} &  & \\, & {e}^{x} & =1 \\\\ {e}^{x} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}) &  & \\, & x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=0$ and $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})$ are the real solutions to the equation."}]}
